  "notes": "The complete official Mojo Manual (docs/site/manual, all .mdx pages: get-started, values/ownership/lifetimes, types, structs, traits, generics, functions, parameters, lifecycle, metaprogramming, pointers, Python interop, GPU, decorators) plus the language reference (docs/site/reference) and top-level docs pages (vision, roadmap, FAQ, pixi, requirements, index, nightly changelog). MDX front matter and markup kept as-is, minimal cleaning only. Excluded: images (PNG), docs/site/code (692,519 chars of runnable .mojo versions of code samples already embedded in the .mdx pages - duplicative), docs/compiler (internal compiler overviews/manual, not language teaching material), docs/contributing and changelog/release notes. Caution: this is the current (post-1.0) Manual, so it matches Mojo 1.x; the community tutorials in the other Mojo files predate 1.0 and use older APIs.",
